  "security_implications": "The combinational logic directly generates the debug policy output (category, valid, relocked). In SocDbgStProd, it blindly passes untrusted shadowed registers from the RoT without integrity checks; a corrupt shadowed value could insert an illegal category (DbgCategory4) or invalid mubi encoding, potentially enabling unauthorized debug. In Blank/PreProd, decode of lc_dft_en_i/lc_hw_debug_en_i relies on lc_tx_test_true_strict with no explicit mubi validity check (though corrupt signals likely lock debug, providing a fail-safe). The default state locks down the policy, but the core risk lies in the unvalidated shadowed path during product state.",
